# NOTE: git does NOT support trailing comments on a pattern line. A line like
# "  .secret-url   # my note  " is treated as a literal filename and silently
# matches nothing. Keep every comment on its own line.

# ── secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# unlisted source-bundle path
.secret-url
# carries SALT; publish worker/wrangler.toml.example instead
worker/wrangler.toml
worker/.dev.vars
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
id_rsa*
.wrangler/

# ── internal ops: infra ids, private host, unlisted URLs ─────────────────
# CLAUDE.md is PUBLIC now (contributor guide). The private operational
# notes live in CLAUDE.local.md and the CLAUDE-*.md sheets: infra ids,
# hosts, unlisted URLs. Those stay ignored.
CLAUDE.local.md
CLAUDE-*.md
README-NEEMA.md
# deploy.sh carries the private origin host and the unlisted source path
deploy.sh

# ── third-party audio: NOT ours to redistribute ──────────────────────────
# The mix is "Ritmos De Los Muertos" by J. Pool and the gritos are sourced
# clips. The art streams them from our own origin; the repo must never carry
# or redistribute them. See ART_DIRECTION.md "Audio and rights".
*.mp3
*.m4a
*.webm
*.wav
*.ogg
gritos/
ritmos-de-los-muertos.*

# ── build + scratch ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
sklz-source.zip
frames/
thumb.png
thumb.webp
clip*.mp4
*.log
node_modules/
.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# agent scratch: browser captures
interceptor-screenshot-*
state/
drain.log

# screensaver build output and fetched vendor headers
screensaver/macos/build/
screensaver/windows/build/
screensaver/windows/vendor/
